Rips_EnterRip
├── when the contract is paused
│   └── it should revert.
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert.
├── when the stake does not exist
│   └── it should revert.
├── when the active rip has expired and the stake is deleted
│   └── it should revert.
├── when the active rip has expired and the stake is not deleted
│   ├── it should create a new rip.
│   └── it should emit a {RipCreated} event.
├── when entry count is zero
│   └── it should revert.
├── given the stake currency is native
│   ├── when the payment amount is incorrect
│   │   └── it should revert.
│   ├── when requested entries are fewer than available
│   │   ├── it should update entries sold count.
│   │   ├── it should store entry ranges for the recipient.
│   │   ├── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
│   │   ├── when recipient is different from the caller
│   │   │   └── it should store entry ranges for the recipient, not the caller.
│   │   └── when entry count exceeds MAX_ENTRIES_PER_RANGE
│   │       └── it should split into multiple entry ranges.
│   ├── when requested entries equal the remaining capacity
│   │   ├── it should purchase all requested entries.
│   │   ├── it should set rip status to SoldOut.
│   │   ├── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
│   │   ├── given the stake is not deleted
│   │   │   └── it should create a new rip for the stake.
│   │   └── given the stake is deleted
│   │       └── it should clear the active rip mapping.
│   └── when requested entries exceed available entries
│       ├── it should purchase only the available entries.
│       ├── it should set rip status to SoldOut.
│       ├── it should refund excess ETH to the caller. TODO: fix test - to recipient
│       └── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
└── given the stake currency is an ERC20 token
    ├── when ETH is sent
    │   └── it should revert.
    ├── when requested entries are fewer than available
    │   ├── it should pull exactly toBuy * entryPrice tokens from the caller.
    │   ├── it should update entries sold count.
    │   ├── it should store entry ranges for the recipient.
    │   ├── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
    │   ├── when recipient is different from the caller
    │   │   └── it should store entry ranges for the recipient, not the caller.
    │   └── when entry count exceeds MAX_ENTRIES_PER_RANGE
    │       └── it should split into multiple entry ranges.
    ├── when requested entries equal the remaining capacity
    │   ├── it should purchase all requested entries.
    │   ├── it should pull exactly entryCap * entryPrice tokens from the caller.
    │   ├── it should set rip status to SoldOut.
    │   └── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
    └── when requested entries exceed available entries
        ├── it should purchase only the available entries.
        ├── it should pull only the available entries cost from the caller.
        ├── it should set rip status to SoldOut.
        └── it should emit a {RipEntered} event.
